.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt MSGGET 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm msgget ,
.Nm msgsnd ,
.Nm msgrcv ,
.Nm msgctl
.Nd System V message queues
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/msg.h
.Ft int
.Fn msgget "key_t key" "int msgflg"
.Ft int
.Fn msgsnd "int msqid" "const void *msgp" "size_t msgsz" "int msgflg"
.Ft ssize_t
.Fn msgrcv "int msqid" "void *msgp" "size_t msgsz" "long msgtyp" "int msgflg"
.Ft int
.Fn msgctl "int msqid" "int cmd" "struct msqid_ds *buf"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A queue holds messages, each a type of at least 1 and up to 8192 bytes of
text, at most 16384 bytes of text in all and as many messages.
.Fn msgget
finds or makes one as
.Xr shmget 2
does a segment, from a table of 64.
.Pp
.Fn msgsnd
appends the message at
.Fa msgp ,
a long type and
.Fa msgsz
bytes of text, waiting while the queue's bytes or its count would pass its
limit, unless
.Dv IPC_NOWAIT .
.Pp
.Fn msgrcv
takes a message into
.Fa msgp :
the first for a
.Fa msgtyp
of 0, the first of that type for a positive one, or with
.Dv MSG_EXCEPT
the first of another, and the first of the lowest type up to its
magnitude for a negative one.
It waits while there is none, unless
.Dv IPC_NOWAIT .
A message longer than
.Fa msgsz
stays and is
.Er E2BIG ,
unless
.Dv MSG_NOERROR
cuts it.
.Dv MSG_COPY
is
.Er ENOSYS ,
as from a Linux built without checkpoint and restore.
.Pp
.Fn msgctl
takes
.Dv IPC_STAT ,
.Dv MSG_STAT ,
.Dv MSG_STAT_ANY ,
.Dv IPC_SET ,
which may raise the queue's byte limit past 16384 only for a privileged
caller,
.Dv IPC_RMID ,
which wakes the waiters with
.Er EIDRM ,
.Dv IPC_INFO
and
.Dv MSG_INFO ,
as
.Xr shmctl 2
takes its own.
.Ss System call interface
The direct calls are numbers 399
.Pq Fn msgget ,
400
.Pq Fn msgsnd ,
401
.Pq Fn msgrcv
and 402
.Pq Fn msgctl ;
musl reaches the same through
.Xr ipc 2 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn msgrcv
returns the bytes of text taken, and the others 0, an id, or what
.Xr shmctl 2
returns for the same commands; on failure -1 with
.Va errno
set.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er E2BIG
A message longer than
.Fa msgsz
without
.Dv MSG_NOERROR .
.It Bq Er EACCES
A send to a queue the caller may not write, or a receive from one it may
not read.
.It Bq Er EAGAIN
A full queue with
.Dv IPC_NOWAIT .
.It Bq Er EIDRM
The queue was removed while the caller waited.
.It Bq Er EINTR
A signal ended the wait.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
A size past 8192, a type below 1, a negative
.Fa msgsz ,
or an id with no queue.
.It Bq Er ENOMSG
No message to take, with
.Dv IPC_NOWAIT .
.It Bq Er ENOSYS
.Dv MSG_COPY .
.It Bq Er EPERM
.Dv IPC_SET
or
.Dv IPC_RMID
from a caller that neither owns nor made the queue, or a byte limit past
16384 from an unprivileged one.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ipc 2 ,
.Xr mq_open 2 ,
.Xr semget 2 ,
.Xr shmget 2 ,
.Xr proc 5
